# Shell scripts must be LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` writes these files
# with CRLF, and a POSIX shell cannot run them: `set -euo pipefail` becomes
# `set -euo pipefail\r` and fails with "invalid option name", and `do\r` is a
# syntax error. Git already stores these blobs with LF, so CI on Linux is
# unaffected -- but the scripts are unrunnable for anyone who checks out on
# Windows, which Layer 0 exercises directly.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Shared contract files must stay byte-identical across repositories.
#
# docs/contracts/README.md requires this directory to match
# `brief/contracts/` byte for byte, and SecurityLab pins the mirrored MCP
# schemas by sha256 (securitylab_mcp/tests/test_contract.py). Git stores these
# blobs with LF, so Linux CI already agrees; a `core.autocrlf=true` checkout
# rewrites them to CRLF and every byte/sha256 comparison outside CI reports a
# spurious drift. Pinning them to LF makes the rule hold on any platform.
docs/contracts/** text eol=lf

# The cross-repo MemoryPack fixture is a verbatim copy of the dsh-memory
# producer's output and is compared byte for byte. Keep it LF so a Windows
# checkout does not rewrite it and break that equality.
fleet/test/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
